A learned decision tree follows branching questions. It is machine learning, but it is not a deep neural network. This record describes that one model; it does not train it.

```javascript
const model = {
  kind: "decision tree",
  machineLearning: true,
  deepLearning: false
};
console.log(model.machineLearning);
console.log(model.deepLearning);
```

It prints true, then false. The two names do not mean the same thing.
